00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.190 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  in India poverty is so pervasive  that you can either decide to forget  about it or you can decide to fight it  you can't ignore it  India has the world's largest child  population  more than 150 million children in the  age group of zero to six years of age  live in India 50 of them go to the free  government system  however if you look at grade 5 and  learning outcomes we find that nearly  half of the kids in India are unable to  read a single paragraph or to do basic  subtraction or division which renders  them unable to do anything for their  informal education or even formal  employment  my goal as a social entrepreneur is to  come up with Solutions and innovations  that really change the fabric of the  world in a way that benefits low income  population and population that nobody is  building anything for essentially we're  trying to change the social fabric of  the country and the Norms of the country  no situation where low income parents  who are majority of the population are  actually going to spend time every day  20 minutes on learning this is a huge  change right you're trying to basically  shift time use patterns of a huge  population onto something that they have  not been doing earlier and so I think  that challenge is what consumes us every  day  [Music]  so I was born to a family of government  officials we lived in smaller parts of  India as well and we could see the  poverty and the lack of opportunities  that others faced but I was lucky that I  was in a middle class family and got the  best out of Education I think from early  age we were cognizant of the privilege  that we've had in terms of great  education the opportunities that that  afforded us and on the flip side the  lack of opportunity that faces more than  five crore or 50 million children today  in the 0 to 6 age group in the country  the more I thought about it and the more  over the last 10 years as I've worked in  the social impact space I felt that the  first six years are where most of your  development happens of your brain and  your body  we're an edtech non-profit working to  help one million children in India so  far with early childhood education  our short-term goal at Rocket learning  is to really comprehensively work  together to help children get up to  speed  rocket learning's approach is to create  these Dynamic digital communities of  parents and preschool teachers to  empower them and Inspire them to be  active participants and enablers in  their child's learning so rocket  learning has created 70 000 WhatsApp  groups which act as Dynamic communities  on which we are able to share some  content that is easy for children to do  in their own homes or in their Learning  Centers you already are on WhatsApp  you're already using it to send messages  to your family etc etc and so through  that 70 000 groups and one million  parents get our content we're able to  then send back nudges and content it's  very personalized for a particular user  a particular group particularly teacher  we have more than 2 000 audiovisual  pieces worksheets etc etc that are then  shared with the Last Mile with parents  and teachers who can then use them in  their daily life  [Music]  the railways are shut the airlines will  soon be shot and Interstate bus travel  is all shut there's a lot of unknowns  about how this is going to play out in  India and the honest truth is nobody  really knows at this point  for close to two years in India and in  fact in the world children did not come  to schools so more schooling actually  shifted to homeschooling for those two  years and so maybe the higher income  child didn't lose out on so much they  also had access to online classes and so  on but low-income children living in  rural parts of the world were not able  to access any sort of online education  for the most part that's where our  programs for engaging parents through  technology actually came into being it's  not rocket science honestly to teach  kids the basic fundamentals you just  need to be able to give some information  to the right person one is parents of  children low income parents secondly we  saw that you know there are these 1.3  million body workers across the country  daycare workers paid by government all  female they feel that they can be  Educators and that they should be  recognized as such and they also feel  that they need support to do a better  job in their classrooms  over the last few years we've been lucky  to see phenomenal impact on the children  parents and preschool teachers who've  been a part of the program  you've seen that for parents there is  very significant Behavior change parents  who are part of our program are actually  engaging twice the number of time and  number of days as you know counterparts  who are not part of the program they  spend a lot more time with the children  they're a lot more confident in their  abilities and for children themselves we  see that they are actually School ready  and life ready by the age of six if  they've gone through the program their  scores on tests improved by 30 or more  but more importantly they actually shift  to the top one third of you know what  they would have been if they were not  part of the program  even Beyond academic skills I think the  most visible signs of impact are when I  go into the field and talk to parents  and angan body workers right and they  tell me that children are not afraid of  going to school anymore they're not  running away they want to go to the  center they're looking forward to these  playful learning activities as opposed  to running away from them they're  confident in what they can do they don't  mind getting up in front of a group and  showcasing what they are able to do and  they have more self-control and ability  to interact with others as well  I think in that way if you go and see  some of these children you really see  them in a very different trajectory from  you know what they were on otherwise  there have been so many times when I  thought that we've bitter off more than  we can show that we're attempting The  Impossible  and in fact a lot of the ecosystem has  told us this as well that why are you  working with parents how are they going  to make a change how are you using  technology in a country that often  doesn't have any but then luckily it's  always been counterbalanced by the  community of users that we've had who've  told us in no uncertain terms that you  know what you're doing is helpful to us  and we want you to continue working with  us  the most significant part about our  success as the rocket learning  organization has been the fact that  we've been able to get a lot of talented  Mission oriented people right from the  beginning who work together without any  ego all with a single-minded focus to  solve the problem  I've been incredibly fortunate in my  personal journey to have family members  parents my spouse siblings who have been  willing to support whatever I do and in  fact who don't think it's a step down to  go into social entrepreneurship from a  corporate career they think that this is  the best thing that I could be doing and  they're proud of me for doing that and  that takes all pressure on you to follow  your dreams  a lot of my personal Journey has been  driven by folks who have supported me  they've known that I'm not going to be  financially as successful as many of my  peers they've thought that what I'm  doing is the best thing that I could be  doing and that I'll change the world and  that's really been a huge support for me  [Music]

